  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving the resilience of food systems  social protection of refugees in Iowara, Western Province, Papua New Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improve the resilience of food systems and social protection of refugees in Iowara will be implemented at the refugee settlement site known as Iowara in Western Province. The Iowara population comprises of approximately 3,000 refugees and a small host population. Despite the majority of refugees arriving in the 1980s, only a small number have been naturalized. The refugee community has received limited integration support and has been left behind in terms of development due to their refugee status, particularly those who with specific needs/vulnerabilities.

The focus will be on improving the resilience of the food systems for the refugee community and the social protection systems for the most vulnerable groups who have been adversely impacted by consecutive crises, including climate hazards, the COVID-19 pandemic and the Ukraine crisis.</narrative>
  </description>
